# Mobile Optimiser Agent

Ensure **mobile stays current with every feature change**. Primary mobile app today = **Capacitor shell** (`apps/capacitor-shell/`) loading the same web UI. Future = **Expo** (`apps/mobile/`) with JWT APIs.

## Authority

- **Capacitor (Option B — production mobile now):** Full web app in WebView; role-based nav from Jinja. Any template/static change **automatically affects Android/iOS** after refresh/sync.
- **Expo (Option A — later):** Native screens; requires `/api/v1` endpoints. See `docs/MOBILE_STRATEGY.md`.
- **Mobile UI stack (global):** `mobile-layout.css`, `mobile-ui.css`, `mobile-layout.js`, `mobile-config.js` loaded from `base.html`.

## Mandatory checklist — user-facing changes

Every change to **templates, static CSS/JS, routes that render HTML, or user-visible APIs**:

1. **Capacitor parity** — Web change = mobile app change. No separate “mobile template” unless documented; fix the shared template.
2. **Extend `base.html`** — New screens must not bypass the mobile stack (`base_clean.html` is not wired for full mobile).
3. **Mobile UI checklist** — Follow `docs/MOBILE_UI_DEVELOPER_CHECKLIST.md` (touch targets, headers, tables, opt-out attributes).
4. **Avoid mobile breakers** — No inline `min-width` on tables; no mouse-only actions; DataTables pages must remain filterable on phone.
5. **Automated check** — Run `python3 scripts/run_mobile_ui_check.py` before marking done (included in `run_agent_approval_loop.py`).
6. **Manual verify** — Test at ≤991px width or on Capacitor emulator/device; force-refresh after CSS/JS changes (no native rebuild needed for static assets).

## API-first (Expo path)

When adding behaviour that Expo will need later:

- [ ] Stable versioned endpoint (`/api/v1` or `/api/v2`)
- [ ] Same auth rules as web (JWT for native; session for Capacitor)
- [ ] Update `docs/MOBILE_STRATEGY.md` API table if contract changes

## Template opt-out attributes

| Attribute | When |
|-----------|------|
| `data-mobile-table="scroll"` | Wide grid must horizontal-scroll, not card layout |
| `data-inertia-no-card="true"` | Never auto card-table |
| `data-inertia-no-wrap="true"` | Do not auto-wrap in scroll region |

## Manual classes

| Class | When |
|-------|------|
| `.mobile-card-table` | Force card rows on phone |
| `.mobile-action-stack` | Full-width stacked buttons |
| `.rec-workflow-mobile` | Rec module: sticky bar + summary grid |

## Feature brief (Mobile Optimiser row)

State explicitly:

- **Capacitor impact:** which templates/static files change
- **Mobile UX:** header/actions/table strategy
- **API (Expo):** new/changed endpoints or N/A
- **Test plan:** `run_mobile_ui_check.py` + manual steps (viewport width / device)

## Invoke

User says "mobile optimiser," "Capacitor," "mobile UI," "phone layout," or edits templates/static/apps/capacitor-shell. @ Mobile Optimiser.

**Do not skip** for backend-only refactors with no user-visible change (state N/A in gate).
